      "Language": "chi",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "This work was done to evaluate the indication, effectiveness, and side effects of internal radiotherapy with radioactive nuclide strontium-89 (89Sr) in patients with malignant metastasis in the bone."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "Fifty-six patients with skeletal metastasis received this internal radiotherapy. The patients were observed and followed up with respect to pain control, lesion improvement and side effects."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "The overall effective rate of pain control was 76.8% with the effective rate of prostatic cancer and breast cancer higher than 80%. The lesions in 81.8% patients as assessed by SPECT imaging, were improved. The mild lowering of white cells, platelets and red cells was the main side effect."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "Internal radiotherapy with 89Sr is very useful for patients with malignant cancer metastasis in the bone."
        }
      ]},
